WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:02.434
-Jack Harlow. Jack, look at us.

00:00:02.434 --> 00:00:04.868
Can I just explain --
You made your TV debut.

00:00:04.868 --> 00:00:06.467
You performed here.

00:00:06.467 --> 00:00:09.567
Now tonight, this is your first
talk show interview.

00:00:09.567 --> 00:00:13.167
So you're debuting your t--
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.167 --> 00:00:15.367
-Yeah.

00:00:15.367 --> 00:00:18.868
Whenever I -- Whenever I
imagined the couch time,

00:00:18.868 --> 00:00:21.300
I was always like, "Oh,
this sounds nerve-wracking."

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:23.434
But I feel -- I feel great.
I actually feel --

00:00:23.434 --> 00:00:24.534
[ Cheers and applause ]
-You feel good?

00:00:24.534 --> 00:00:28.100
You feel comfy?
-I feel at ease with you.

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:29.501
-Good.
That's what I want you to do.

00:00:29.501 --> 00:00:32.467
Good, 'cause you know
I love you, man.

00:00:32.467 --> 00:00:35.801
You're one of the biggest
rappers on the planet right now.

00:00:35.801 --> 00:00:38.968
And I just --
I have this photo of your --

00:00:38.968 --> 00:00:41.701
This is a performance
that someone took a photo of.

00:00:41.701 --> 00:00:44.100
This is one of your --
-Wyatt, my best friend,

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:45.334
took that photo.

00:00:45.334 --> 00:00:47.901
-This is one of your
first gigs I guess?

00:00:47.901 --> 00:00:49.100
Yeah?

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:50.300
-My first ever show
in Birmingham, Alabama.

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:51.834
My first ever tour show.

00:00:51.834 --> 00:00:54.801
[ Cheers and applause ]
-This is the tour.

00:00:54.801 --> 00:00:56.868
One, two, three, four, five.

00:00:56.868 --> 00:00:58.434
There's like 10 people there.

00:00:58.434 --> 00:01:00.267
They're not even looking at you,
these guys.

00:01:00.267 --> 00:01:03.300
They're talking to each other --
"Hey, what's up, man?

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:06.334
What do you think of
the concert?"

00:01:06.334 --> 00:01:11.834
How does it feel to go
from here to here?

00:01:11.834 --> 00:01:15.400
-It's validating.

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:17.834
I think I just like --
I appreciate it.

00:01:17.834 --> 00:01:19.100
You know, I appreciate it.

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:20.801
It's fragile to me.

00:01:20.801 --> 00:01:22.634
I know I worked for it.

00:01:22.634 --> 00:01:24.267
I don't take it for granted
at all because of that.

00:01:24.267 --> 00:01:26.167
Because I did everything, bro.

00:01:26.167 --> 00:01:27.634
I did the open mics.

00:01:27.634 --> 00:01:30.300
I did A3Cs.

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:32.868
I begged people to rock with me.

00:01:32.868 --> 00:01:34.634
-Yeah.
-You know what I'm saying?

00:01:34.634 --> 00:01:36.667
I really put in the work.

00:01:36.667 --> 00:01:37.701
-You put the hustle in.

00:01:37.701 --> 00:01:38.934
-So I can always
stand on that.

00:01:38.934 --> 00:01:40.834
You know, no one can say
this was gifted to me.

00:01:40.834 --> 00:01:45.267
-Yeah, good man. I agree.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:45.267 --> 00:01:47.701
You start here.

00:01:47.701 --> 00:01:49.934
I mean, honestly, you should be
friends with all these people.

00:01:49.934 --> 00:01:51.767
There's only 10 people there.

00:01:51.767 --> 00:01:56.033
-You know what's crazy is I went
back to Birmingham in the fall.

00:01:56.033 --> 00:01:58.367
We sold it out in three seconds.

00:01:58.367 --> 00:02:02.801
[ Cheers and applause ]
Thank you. Thank you.

00:02:02.801 --> 00:02:06.667
And, like, maybe seven of
the people were there

00:02:06.667 --> 00:02:09.400
from this photo,
this show in the this fall,

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:10.767
and they had on
the same outfits.

00:02:10.767 --> 00:02:12.634
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.634 --> 00:02:14.734
-That's a good move.
That's awesome.

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:16.934
Oh, I love they did that.
Birmingham, shout-out.

00:02:16.934 --> 00:02:17.968
That's so cool.
-Yeah, I hugged --

00:02:17.968 --> 00:02:19.334
I met some of them
after the show.

00:02:19.334 --> 00:02:20.934
We took pictures and reminisced.

00:02:20.934 --> 00:02:22.434
-I mean, you start here,

00:02:22.434 --> 00:02:25.033
then you end up performing
at the Grammys

00:02:25.033 --> 00:02:26.934
with Lil Nas X,
doing "Industry Baby."

00:02:26.934 --> 00:02:29.200
Come on, hit number one.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:33.467 --> 00:02:37.000
What does it feel like to have
a number-one song?

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:38.701
Did you know it was gonna
be a hit?

00:02:38.701 --> 00:02:40.601
-"Industry Baby"?
-Yeah.

00:02:40.601 --> 00:02:42.501
-I knew "Industry Baby" was
gonna be special.

00:02:42.501 --> 00:02:43.901
In fact, when I was writing
the verse,

00:02:43.901 --> 00:02:45.634
everyone in the room,
I kept saying,

00:02:45.634 --> 00:02:48.033
"This is gonna be a number one.
This is gonna be --"

00:02:48.033 --> 00:02:50.834
I was like, "This is gonna be
a number one, trust me, y'all."

00:02:50.834 --> 00:02:52.334
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:02:52.334 --> 00:02:55.701
-And what's it like performing
with Lil Nas X?

00:02:55.701 --> 00:02:58.400
-You gotta bring your A game
to stand out.

00:02:58.400 --> 00:02:59.801
You know what I mean?
-Yeah, exactly.

00:02:59.801 --> 00:03:01.300
It's hard to take the light
off that guy.

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:03.300
-He's just so powerful.

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:06.067
I had eight bars at the Grammys.

00:03:06.067 --> 00:03:09.534
And so he had this massive head.
-He does it up.

00:03:09.534 --> 00:03:12.434
-He had this massive Lil Nas X
head that was on the stage.

00:03:12.434 --> 00:03:15.734
Like, his face, and I was
hiding inside of it

00:03:15.734 --> 00:03:17.234
waiting for my time
to come out.

00:03:17.234 --> 00:03:18.434
[ Laughter ]

00:03:18.434 --> 00:03:21.033
-What part of
the head did you come out of?

00:03:21.033 --> 00:03:22.367
-The back of it.
-Yeah.

00:03:22.367 --> 00:03:23.567
[ Laughter ]

00:03:23.567 --> 00:03:25.067
-Yeah, he's got a great head,
man.

00:03:25.067 --> 00:03:26.133
-Yeah, he's got a great head.

00:03:26.133 --> 00:03:27.567
He really does.
He really does.

00:03:27.567 --> 00:03:29.033
-So, I came out the back of it.

00:03:29.033 --> 00:03:31.901
The whole time I'm inside,
I'm just thinking --

00:03:31.901 --> 00:03:33.667
The whole time
I'm inside his head,

00:03:33.667 --> 00:03:35.801
I'm just thinking like,

00:03:35.801 --> 00:03:38.667
"I got to kill this."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:38.667 --> 00:03:40.334
-This whole moment has been
crafted by him,

00:03:40.334 --> 00:03:44.400
so I got to come out swinging.

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:46.067
-I want to say the last month,
or something,

00:03:46.067 --> 00:03:47.234
since this album came out,

00:03:47.234 --> 00:03:49.834
every video I see you
do goes viral.

00:03:49.834 --> 00:03:52.000
There's something else
crazy happening.

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:53.801
And I just want to see
if you can give me

00:03:53.801 --> 00:03:55.834
your thoughts
on a few of these, right?

00:03:55.834 --> 00:03:57.901
This first one is a clip of you
getting interviewed

00:03:57.901 --> 00:03:59.834
at the Met Gala
that we were just talking about.

00:03:59.834 --> 00:04:01.501
Do you guys know
what I'm talking about?

00:04:01.501 --> 00:04:04.000
[ Cheers and applause ]
-They've seen it.

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:05.300
They've seen it.

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:07.000
-Yeah, I know, but I think
we should see it again.

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:08.200
We have to play it.

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:11.567
Emma Chamberlain, okay,
is interviewing you.

00:04:11.567 --> 00:04:15.334
And watch her reaction
and watch what you say.

00:04:15.334 --> 00:04:17.033
-I'll see you in there.
-Can't wait.

00:04:17.033 --> 00:04:18.100
Love you.
Bye.

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:23.634
-Love ya.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:23.634 --> 00:04:27.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:27.634 --> 00:04:30.467
-Is that the effect?
Like, what is that?

00:04:30.467 --> 00:04:34.634
Is that the Harlow effect
or what is it?

00:04:34.634 --> 00:04:36.367
-That's like a piece of art
because there's so many ways

00:04:36.367 --> 00:04:38.300
to interpret that,
you know what I mean?

00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:39.701
[ Laughter ]

00:04:39.701 --> 00:04:42.100
Everyone has a different take on
what was going through her head.

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:43.767
So I'll leave it up
to interpretation.

00:04:43.767 --> 00:04:45.000
-Yeah.

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:48.000
But do you leave every interview
saying "love you"?

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:50.868
-Only if I love them.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:50.868 --> 00:04:52.801
-Alright. Alright.
You loved her.

00:04:52.801 --> 00:04:57.000
-I have a lot of warmth
to share.

00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:59.400
-You saying, "love ya"
was just genuine.

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:01.868
And then her reaction is like,
"Ha. Huh?"

00:05:01.868 --> 00:05:03.601
[ Laughter ]

00:05:03.601 --> 00:05:05.000
-You forgot the part
where she said it back.

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:07.501
We love each other.
-Yeah, hey.

00:05:07.501 --> 00:05:09.133
Then you were
at the Celtics game.

00:05:09.133 --> 00:05:10.601
-Yeah.
-Okay.

00:05:10.601 --> 00:05:11.767
-That was just --

00:05:11.767 --> 00:05:14.701
-So, they show you
on the jumbotron.

00:05:14.701 --> 00:05:17.167
And then the refs are talking
to each other,

00:05:17.167 --> 00:05:19.300
and their mics were on.

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:23.534
Take a look at this.
-Who's Jack Harlow?

00:05:23.534 --> 00:05:24.901
Who's Jack Harlow?

00:05:24.901 --> 00:05:26.300
-I have no idea.
-The guy over here.

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:28.501
Right here.
He's in the white shirt.

00:05:28.501 --> 00:05:31.200
-Yeah, who is he?
-I don't know.

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:32.434
Go ask him.

00:05:32.434 --> 00:05:40.934
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:40.934 --> 00:05:43.467
-"Go ask him."
"Who's Jack Harlow?"

00:05:43.467 --> 00:05:44.968
"I don't know.
Go ask him."

00:05:44.968 --> 00:05:46.434
[ Laughter ]

00:05:46.434 --> 00:05:49.601
You had a funny reaction to that
because clearly they didn't see

00:05:49.601 --> 00:05:53.033
"Chronicles of Narnia"
or something like that.

00:05:53.033 --> 00:05:54.968
-Yeah, there's a portion
of this crowd that knows

00:05:54.968 --> 00:05:57.133
that I get compared
to that half goat from "Narnia."

00:05:57.133 --> 00:05:58.634
[ Laughter ]

00:05:58.634 --> 00:06:01.968
We have the same
sort of thing going right here.

00:06:01.968 --> 00:06:03.968
-Yeah.
-No, it was wild.

00:06:03.968 --> 00:06:07.033
I was like -- Of course
I'm not watching the broadcast.

00:06:07.033 --> 00:06:08.601
And then people start blowing up
my phone like,

00:06:08.601 --> 00:06:11.434
"Yo, the refs have no idea
who you are."

00:06:11.434 --> 00:06:14.067
I'm like, "Okay."
-Yeah, who cares?

00:06:14.067 --> 00:06:15.367
-I got online,
and I'm seeing the clip.

00:06:15.367 --> 00:06:17.400
I think the clip is iconic.

00:06:17.400 --> 00:06:18.868
So, I'm like,
I've got to let this guy know

00:06:18.868 --> 00:06:20.634
who I am, Scott Foster.
-Yeah.

00:06:20.634 --> 00:06:23.200
-So, it's the fourth quarter
and he's over on the sideline.

00:06:23.200 --> 00:06:24.701
And he comes over.

00:06:24.701 --> 00:06:28.734
And I'm like, "Yo," and
I'm trying to get his attention.

00:06:28.734 --> 00:06:31.067
He's like, "My daughter
already texted me."

00:06:31.067 --> 00:06:35.033
[ Laughter ]
-"I know.

00:06:35.033 --> 00:06:36.267
My daughter already texted me.

00:06:36.267 --> 00:06:37.868
I know the who heck you are."

00:06:40.901 --> 00:06:44.434
Now, you got cast in your first
big movie, bud,

00:06:44.434 --> 00:06:46.501
which I'm excited about
'cause you got a good look.

00:06:46.501 --> 00:06:48.167
This is just the start.

00:06:48.167 --> 00:06:49.334
You are going to be
in the remake of

00:06:49.334 --> 00:06:51.000
"White Men Can't Jump."

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:53.467
[ Cheers and applause ]
I love this.

00:06:53.467 --> 00:06:54.801
I love this.

00:06:54.801 --> 00:06:57.067
How did you get involved
with it,

00:06:57.067 --> 00:06:58.934
and do you know the movie?

00:06:58.934 --> 00:07:00.367
Do you know the original?

00:07:00.367 --> 00:07:01.734
-Yeah, I know about it.

00:07:01.734 --> 00:07:04.934
[ Laughter ]
I had heard about it.

00:07:04.934 --> 00:07:07.467
I mean, I know how iconic it is.

00:07:07.467 --> 00:07:10.100
Then when I got the offer, I was
like, "Hm, I should watch it."

00:07:10.100 --> 00:07:11.701
[ Laughter ]

00:07:11.701 --> 00:07:13.367
To be fair, it came out
before I was born.

00:07:13.367 --> 00:07:14.467
So, I watched it.

00:07:14.467 --> 00:07:16.501
I see why it's classic.
-Yeah.

00:07:16.501 --> 00:07:19.267
-It's not as gimmicky
as I might have imagined.

00:07:19.267 --> 00:07:21.868
-Oh, it's funny.
-Phenomenal dialogue.

00:07:21.868 --> 00:07:24.400
So I'm excited.
We got the offer.

00:07:24.400 --> 00:07:27.434
Kenya Barris called D.J. Drama,
who I'm signed to.

00:07:27.434 --> 00:07:28.567
Drama called me, he's like,
"Hey, you want

00:07:28.567 --> 00:07:29.801
to be in this movie?"

00:07:29.801 --> 00:07:31.100
-Kenya Barris is amazing.
He's talented.

00:07:31.100 --> 00:07:33.234
-Yeah, shout-out, Kenya.

00:07:33.234 --> 00:07:34.934
-You're playing
the Woody Harrelson role.

00:07:34.934 --> 00:07:35.968
-That's right.

00:07:35.968 --> 00:07:38.033
-Have you talked to Woody
at all?

00:07:38.033 --> 00:07:40.567
-No. I want to.

00:07:40.567 --> 00:07:42.968
I want his co-sign.

00:07:42.968 --> 00:07:44.968
I want him to tell me like,
"You can do it."

00:07:44.968 --> 00:07:47.434
-Oh, yeah,
I think Woody would do that.

00:07:47.434 --> 00:07:49.734
You have to talk to him.
You have to meet him.

00:07:49.734 --> 00:07:51.968
-Yeah, I feel like he's about
to come out or something.

00:07:51.968 --> 00:07:54.934
-No, I wouldn't do that to you.
I wouldn't do that.

00:07:54.934 --> 00:07:56.133
I wouldn't do that to you,
I'm sorry.

00:07:56.133 --> 00:07:57.200
I wouldn't -- I'm sorry.

00:07:57.200 --> 00:07:58.400
-That's how you
always lead it up.

00:07:58.400 --> 00:07:59.601
-I know. I'm sorry.
I just get excited.

00:07:59.601 --> 00:08:01.968
-"So, have you talked to him?"
-No, no, no.

00:08:01.968 --> 00:08:04.901
He pops up like,
"Hey, how you doing?"

00:08:04.901 --> 00:08:06.167
He's not here.
He's not here.

00:08:06.167 --> 00:08:08.300
Woody, don't come out yet.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:11.067
He's been under there
the whole time.

00:08:11.067 --> 00:08:12.601
-No woodys under there.
-No, wait, no, no.

00:08:12.601 --> 00:08:22.601
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:24.234 --> 00:08:25.334
I just walked
right into that one.

00:08:25.334 --> 00:08:26.767
I just walked right
into that one.

00:08:26.767 --> 00:08:27.901
I just walked right into it.
-That's okay.

00:08:27.901 --> 00:08:29.567
We've had a couple.
-Yeah.

00:08:30.701 --> 00:08:32.667
[ Laughter ]
-"Come Home the Kids Miss You."

00:08:32.667 --> 00:08:34.734
This is out,
just came out Friday.

00:08:34.734 --> 00:08:36.033
Can you tell us about the title?

00:08:36.033 --> 00:08:38.267
"Come Home the Kids Miss You"?

00:08:38.267 --> 00:08:41.067
-I just want to give a shout-out
to my supporters because

00:08:41.067 --> 00:08:43.367
they kind of supplied me
with this title.

00:08:43.367 --> 00:08:46.367
I was seeing under my comments
for a while,

00:08:46.367 --> 00:08:48.834
all my posts,
fans were commenting,

00:08:48.834 --> 00:08:50.534
"Come home, the kids miss you."

00:08:50.534 --> 00:08:52.901
I just thought it was
such a poetic line.

00:08:52.901 --> 00:08:55.634
And then I just -- When I was
sitting and I was like,

00:08:55.634 --> 00:08:57.400
"Yo, I need to come up
with an album title."

00:08:57.400 --> 00:08:59.767
I realized I spent so much time
away from home

00:08:59.767 --> 00:09:01.934
during the making of the album,
and just being swept off

00:09:01.934 --> 00:09:03.200
my feet,
being taken around the world,

00:09:03.200 --> 00:09:06.267
so I feel like it
encapsulates this era for me.

00:09:06.267 --> 00:09:09.367
So we went with it.
-Yeah. You crushed it, buddy.

00:09:09.367 --> 00:09:11.400
You got some good features
on here.

00:09:11.400 --> 00:09:14.701
Pharrell, Justin Timberlake.

00:09:14.701 --> 00:09:18.100
[ Cheers and applause ]
-That's your guy.

00:09:18.100 --> 00:09:19.300
-That's my dude, man.

00:09:19.300 --> 00:09:22.501
Lil Wayne. Drake.

00:09:22.501 --> 00:09:24.334
I just saw you
at the Kentucky Derby.

00:09:24.334 --> 00:09:26.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:26.567 --> 00:09:28.834
Is there any coincidence
that you released your album

00:09:28.834 --> 00:09:31.033
the same weekend
as the Kentucky Derby?

00:09:31.033 --> 00:09:32.067
-It's not a coincidence.

00:09:32.067 --> 00:09:33.701
-Yeah, exactly.
-Had to come home.

00:09:33.701 --> 00:09:35.601
-That's a Kentucky boy
right there.

00:09:35.601 --> 00:09:36.901
Congrats on everything, man.

00:09:36.901 --> 00:09:38.234
You know we love you, man.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:38.234 --> 00:09:41.400
It's your first talk show
appearance and you nailed it.

00:09:41.400 --> 00:09:42.501
So happy for you, bud.

00:09:42.501 --> 00:09:43.968
-Appreciate you.
-Very talented guy.

00:09:43.968 --> 00:09:47.601
Jack Harlow, "Come Home the Kids
Miss You" is out right now.

00:09:47.601 --> 00:09:49.400
Jack is performing for us
after the break.

00:09:49.400 --> 00:09:50.467
Come on back.

